==Enemy==
The bane of many debuffers, Loris has a moderately damaging attack which consists of him detaching his sunglasses-like eyes, revealing another, identical pair underneath, jumping into the air, and throwing them into your backlines. He can be treated like a Relic variant of [[Tackey]], but is more dangerous for his Long Distance [[Curse]] than his damage output, as the effect lasts just long enough for him to effectively perma-Curse your ranged attackers. Although he deals less damage, he has more than double the health and knockbacks of Tackey, significantly bolstering his survivability.

When buffed to 150% or more, Loris can potentially become more threatening, although that is mostly dependent on the stage in question. Loris' DPH does remain underwhelming at ~9,000 damage, and his DPS sits at a laughable ~1,800, but he gains more survivability as he has 560,000 or more health now. This makes him a tad more detrimental to you as it will be harder to knock him back, so he will help the enemies push more.

==Strategy==
Loris will curse your backlines with his range and stop some of your attackers from using their abilities (Massive Damage, Slow, Freeze, etc.) and thus can cripple your army. Your best bet is to rely on attackers that are [[:Category:Cats with Curse Immunity|Immune to Curse]] or can enter his blind spot, like [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Elder Beast Naala]] or [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]. Still, he isn't too hard to deal with thanks to his light (for a Relic) damage and slowish attack speed. Being a Long Distance enemy, you should choose to use shorter-ranged [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rusher]] units, as they often are able to invade Loris' blind spot.

